{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444614-so-why-do-the-wendigo-call-themsevles-that-anyway","id":1444614,"title":"So why do the Wendigo call themsevles that, anyway?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-19T02:30:52-07:00","id":1444614,"title":"So why do the Wendigo call themsevles that, anyway?","content":"A wendigo is a spirit of greed, and has an emaciated appearance with no resemblance to a wolf or werewolf. Why name themselves after a spirit of greed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T02:41:58-07:00","id":1444616,"title":"","content":"Younger Brother are named after their totem which only bears a very passing resemblance to the folkloric W-word and touches much more strongly on secondary sources like August Derleths Ithaqua than the primary Algonquian sources.<br /> <br /> So the primary aspects emphasised were cold, wind and consumption of human flesh rather than the warning nature of the actual lore.<br /> <br /> Edit: Basically, it was the early 90s. For much the same reasons of lack of research Older Brother is also named after their tribal totem though at least that particular term for a particular Horned Serpent mythology isn't as bad form to say out loud as Younger Brothers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":479,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","user":"Damian May","date":". 04-19-2021, 05:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T08:57:25-07:00","id":1444666,"title":"","content":"Because they were named by white authors who had a pop-culture understanding of Native American mythology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26415-cultofjimmy","name":"CultofJimmy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T12:43:58-07:00","id":1444700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CultofJimmy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444614-so-why-do-the-wendigo-call-themsevles-that-anyway?p=1444666#post1444666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because they were named by white authors who had a pop-culture understanding of Native American mythology.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why I wouldn't be surprised if they both got rolled into a singular group in W5 much like the Carna did in V5","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T12:51:24-07:00","id":1444703,"title":"","content":"Garou often have different perspectives than humans on creatures of legend. It's not just the Wendigo. Look at Fenris. Humans see Fenris as an evil figure related to Jormungandr who will lead to the destruction of the world. To the Garou, Fenris is a noble, though ferocious, spirit who is an enemy to Jormungandr. There are other spirits that are similar. You reconcile real world myth and legend to the Garou's version by saying that the human perspective is incomplete and ignorant while the Garou's version is more correct, and here are the reasons why the human version is &quot;incorrect&quot;.<br /> <br /> For my games, this is how I describe the Wendigo spirit. It's a spirit of survival in a harsh winter environment. So while it teaches survival, it is also very harsh itself. Harsh teachers provide harsh lessons so that their children learn what they need in order to avoid calamity when it really matters. But the spirit has certain taboos it punishes, and one of those is cannibalism, even survival cannibalism. It punishes people who engage in it. (In my chronicles, while other tribes often believe the Wendigo violate the Litany against man eating because of their misconceptions of the Wendigo spirit, the tribe actually has the least problems with man eating of all the tribes precisely because their totem is completely against it).<br /> <br /> The game Wendigo itself is not actually a spirit of cannibalism. This is actually made explicit in Ways of the Wolf which introduced the False Wendigo spirit. The False Wendigo was once part of Wendigo's brood, but was corrupted by the Wyrm, and it is this False Wendigo spirit that humans identify with the wendigo myths. Unfortunately, this was not built on in the actual tribebooks which instead attempted a different means to reconcile game lore and human legend, and I think it wasn't very successful. The entire story about Sasquatch and Wendigo was unneccesarily complicated and muddied the waters rather than clarifying things.<br /> <br /> In other words, the creature of legend you identify as a spirit of greed is not Wendigo, it is one of the False Wendigo.<br /> <br /> The actual Wendigo tribal totem does not correspond with the real Native American legends, though there is of course a lot of overlaps. That Garou tribe took Wendigo as their tribal totem because it is a valuable spirit ally to have in a place like northern North America.<br /> <br /> So why did the developers name this tribe after the wendigo? For the same reasons they used Fenris for one of the tribes. It was a known creature of legend and folklore, identifiable with a geographic area, that provided an easy hook to base a Garou tribe around. Simply by association, you know any werewolf tribe associated with the name &quot;Wendigo&quot; has ties to harsh winters, is located around Canada, and is probably a group of fierce fighters. And that is how the tribe is presented. For whatever problems you may have with Wendigo, at least it is a lot more coherent than the Chimera spirit and its tribe the Stargazers, as that spirit has practically nothing in common with the actual Greek legend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T13:41:36-07:00","id":1444709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444614-so-why-do-the-wendigo-call-themsevles-that-anyway?p=1444700#post1444700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is why I wouldn't be surprised if they both got rolled into a singular group in W5 much like the Carna did in V5</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you mean the Hecata.<br /> <br /> But I would be surprised since V5 was collapsing a bunch of bloodlines into a main Clan, instead of trying to merge main Clans together.<br /> <br /> -------------<br /> <br /> I had some how W5 would address this topic in a meaningful fashion since they made a point to bring on a Native American RPG designer who feels pretty strongly about fixing these sorts of things; but with Paradox being Paradox it's unclear if that contribution is still going to be part of things after the last shakeup.<br /> <br /> We know the people involved in make W5 are aware of the fact that WtA is the way it is because of the ignorance of its creators. It seems unlikely that they're going to make large changes to the character of the Tribes, but hopefully they can do something to address things like terminology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T12:32:52-07:00","id":1444899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444614-so-why-do-the-wendigo-call-themsevles-that-anyway?p=1444709#post1444709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you mean the Hecata.<br /> <br /> But I would be surprised since V5 was collapsing a bunch of bloodlines into a main Clan, instead of trying to merge main Clans together.<br /> <br /> -------------<br /> <br /> I had some how W5 would address this topic in a meaningful fashion since they made a point to bring on a Native American RPG designer who feels pretty strongly about fixing these sorts of things; but with Paradox being Paradox it's unclear if that contribution is still going to be part of things after the last shakeup.<br /> <br /> We know the people involved in make W5 are aware of the fact that WtA is the way it is because of the ignorance of its creators. It seems unlikely that they're going to make large changes to the character of the Tribes, but hopefully they can do something to address things like terminology.</div> </div> </div> </div>I heard that their changing all of the indigenous tribes names .Younger brother because their basically calling themselves the Garou equivalent of Voldemort or nylanteop and Crotan because it is based on a racist conspiracy theory against race mixing , and collapsing the indigenous werewolf\u2019s into one tribe sounds even more racist as indigenous people have more then one culture. At least werewolf had 3 different indigenous splats 4 if you count the nuwishia , which is better because it shows different cultures.<br /> <br /> And many missionary\u2019s did compare the W*digo to werewolves latter folklore even had them killed with a silver bullet. But yeah while their where some positive/neutral folklore about Werewolves in the west. See \u201cthe wolf of god\u201d and Biscelent. The hungry winter creature is always portrayed as bad, and in Apocalypse terms basically a bane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T13:43:46-07:00","id":1444910,"title":"","content":"Something I've gone on about at length before, is that beyond changing the terminology, there's not a whole lot you can do without overhauling WtA with a full on reboot. Even then you face a tough choice: You can make the Tribes more global to reduce a lot of the more problematic issues with linking some of them so tightly to specific (and frequently very pop-culture versions of) real world cultures, but then you lose a lot of the representational aspect of having prominent groups within the game that are focused on indigenous cultures. If you want to make sure all the Tribes are doing more to positively center the plights of indigenous and marginalized peoples, 13 Tribes is never going to be enough to do so without tossing groups together that comes off as insensitive.<br /> <br /> You can try to split the difference like Forsaken did (Tribes are global spiritual philosophies which strains the word tribe pretty hard, with Lodges being subgroups within the Tribes that can be customized towards tackling whatever issues you want to focus on), but it's hard to avoid that really falling to one side or the other in how people end up playing the game.<br /> <br /> And you have to deal with the issue of the well-intentioned move to use the Fera to add representation to groups the Garou don't cover only creates an air of exoticism where wanting to play an indigenous person from huge swathes of the world means you have to play a special character type that isn't designed to play nicely with the main PC types.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T14:59:17-07:00","id":1444923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444614-so-why-do-the-wendigo-call-themsevles-that-anyway#post1444614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A wendigo is a spirit of greed, and has an emaciated appearance with no resemblance to a wolf or werewolf. Why name themselves after a spirit of greed?</div> </div> </div> </div>In-universe, Native Americans think of Wendigo as murderous exterminators of lives and cannibals. They thus applied the name for the tribe of Garou as a monster.<br /> <br /> Because, as later books state, the Wendigo's history of the &quot;Pure Lands&quot; is complete bullshit.<br /> <br /> Its the same with vampires. In-universe, the Caine Myth comes from them not Judaism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T16:05:31-07:00","id":1444945,"title":"","content":"That the Theriom argument Phipps, not to do a personal attack or anything but you seem to be very defensive of anything white wolf or Ornyx path ever wrote from having the Technocracy be based on some originally very anti-Semitic conspiracy theories I guess it\u2019s supose to be a satire on those conspiracy theories despite the fact that in first edition the Technocracy being played mostly straight? And having them actually be a very power organization that secretly controls the world with mind control powers? And think \u201cZorder\u201d is a slur?<br /> <br /> White Wolf seriously failed in researching Native cultures","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T17:00:55-07:00","id":1444960,"title":"","content":"I think it's also very important to highlight how dangerous the &quot;everything this group of people believes is a lie so our monsters can make sense in the setting,&quot; is as a tool to use.<br /> <br /> Whatever framework you want to consider this under (satire and punching up not down, creating a fun setting for as many people as possible, etc.), someone is going to be massively turned off to be singled out as being declared invalid in the setting because their people get everything wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T17:14:16-07:00","id":1444963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444614-so-why-do-the-wendigo-call-themsevles-that-anyway?p=1444945#post1444945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That the Theriom argument Phipps, not to do a personal attack or anything but you seem to be very defensive of anything white wolf or Ornyx path ever wrote from having the Technocracy be based on some originally very anti-Semitic conspiracy theories</div> </div> </div> </div>The (1st Edition) Technocracy is a fascist anti-Semitic organization that allied with the Nazis and includes Pogrom (Anti-Jewish) as part of its official terminology. It's why I don't approve of making them player characters unless the players fully understand it is a fascist organization. It's a very dumb idea saying they're based on Anit-Semitic conspiracies when the organization is very solidly an embodiment of Western racism and capitalism. I am DEEPLY suspicious of people who attempt to whitewash the organization and attempts to make it so it is not a strike against Western anti-Judaism and racism.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I guess it\u2019s supose to be a satire on those conspiracy theories despite the fact that in first edition the Technocracy being played mostly straight? And having them actually be a very power organization that secretly controls the world with mind control powers? And think \u201cZorder\u201d is a slur? </div> </div> </div>I think the (1st Edition) Tecnocracy is a bunch of Nazis. I worry about people who try to make them the good guys of Mage. I mean, there's a reason that the religious and brown people of the setting hate the Union.<br /> <br /> Making an anti-fascist work like Mage into anti-Jewish is pretty hard when, again, its a bunch of murderous military anti-democratic eugenicists versus a bunch of oppressed religious people.<br /> <br /> It's pretty hard for me to understand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-20-2021, 08:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T17:17:41-07:00","id":1444964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444614-so-why-do-the-wendigo-call-themsevles-that-anyway?p=1444960#post1444960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's also very important to highlight how dangerous the &quot;everything this group of people believes is a lie so our monsters can make sense in the setting,&quot; is as a tool to use.<br /> <br /> Whatever framework you want to consider this under (satire and punching up not down, creating a fun setting for as many people as possible, etc.), someone is going to be massively turned off to be singled out as being declared invalid in the setting because their people get everything wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the part where we miss each other is, &quot;What do you mean it's a lie?&quot; I mean, werewolves are monsters who used to conduct a millennia-long genocide. The use of Wendigo as a name is a sign that werewolves are MONSTERS. It's a nice reminder that it is not a purely Western myth. And that their name has gone down in history as a thing to be FEARED.<br /> <br /> Are people playing Wendigo as good guys?<br /> <br /> Unless you are kinfolk, everyone is instinctually afraid of you because you are a creature to be feared.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-20-2021, 08:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T18:34:38-07:00","id":1444974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444614-so-why-do-the-wendigo-call-themsevles-that-anyway?p=1444963#post1444963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The (1st Edition) Technocracy is a fascist anti-Semitic organization that allied with the Nazis and includes Pogrom (Anti-Jewish) as part of its official terminology.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's nothing specific anti-Semitic about the in-universe policies of the Technocracy. Mage has also fairly consistently painted Nazism as something that wasn't a Technocracy thing, and that there were plenty of Tradition mages with Nazi sympathies. The Technocracy also aren't fascists (being neither far-right or nationalists in their ideology) but a form of totalitarian left-wing ideology. It's important to remember that Mage is not a right-wing vs. left-wing conflict, but a totalitarian vs. pluralism conflict. <br /> <br /> Pogrom is also a Russian word, not an anti-Jewish slur. It's history is tied closely to Russian violence against Jews, but was also used more broadly to address violence against other minority communities during the same period of heightened violence in the Russian empire. A group that willingly uses it is still morally bankrupt, but this doesn't really address the out-of-game issues with how the Technocracy is written to play into anti-Semitic stereotypes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's a very dumb idea saying they're based on Anit-Semitic conspiracies when the organization is very solidly an embodiment of Western racism and capitalism. I am DEEPLY suspicious of people who attempt to whitewash the organization and attempts to make it so it is not a strike against Western anti-Judaism and racism. </div> </div> </div>Just to remind the conversation: I'm Jewish. This matters to me, a lot.<br /> <br /> It isn't dumb to say the Technocracy is based on anti-Semitic conspiracy theories, <b>because they are</b>. I am deeply suspicious of anyone that wants to engage with this topic and cannot recognize that this can be true despite the intentions of the authors not to make it so. Just like the WtA 1e authors didn't mean to make offensive Native American focused Tribes, but they did.<br /> <br /> The disconnect here seems to be that you're talking about the in-universe element that is the Technocracy, while Konrad and I are talking about the out-of-universe element of the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> You also seem to be struggling with an illogical but simple truth: bigotry is not based in reason. One of the difficulties with non-minority writers writing for minority groups is not understanding how it feels to be attacked from both sides. Bigots are not trying to logically make the case about the targets of their hate, they're justifying hate with ad hoc rationales. There is a long, long, long history of thing involving hypocritical stereotyping. The targets of bigotry are painted as being pathetic and weak so they can be view as inferior and lesser, but also dangerous and strong to be threatening. The goal is to ingrain disgust and fear of the Other in the population so they accept violence (political, verbal, physical and more) as normal, necessary, and just.<br /> <br /> Western conspiracy theories that the Technocracy is based on are irrevocably linked to anti-Semitic bigotry in the West: Jews, because they are cowardly and lacking in moral strength, operate in shadowy cabals (and lets remember where that word comes from!) to secretly undermine good Christians through manipulate and theft... but are also deviously intelligent, wealthy beyond measure, and control everything you don't like in society (banks, taxes, government, media, etc.) so you have to use direct violence to free yourself from their insidious influence.<br /> <br /> What does the Technocracy do? Well, they're moral cowards that deny the truth, and send dupes, cutouts, and other unknowing pawns to do the dirty work of their leaders who stay in the shadows. They attack traditional institutions they don't like, and secretly control the world to influence every part of your life. If you don't understand the parallels... I'm not sure what to say.<br /> <br /> Sometimes authors try to attack a bad institution, but end up either doing more harm to those oppressed by that institution by making said institution seem justified. That's something the Technocracy's creators are guilty of; just like WtA's creators are guilty of perpetuating harmful stereotypes about Native Americans while trying to do the opposite.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Making an anti-fascist work like Mage into anti-Jewish is pretty hard when, again, its a bunch of murderous military anti-democratic eugenicists versus a bunch of oppressed religious people.<br /> <br /> It's pretty hard for me to understand. </div> </div> </div>Let me try to help:<br /> <br /> Satyros Brucato has said that the reason M20 didn't update the Lions of Zion, is because he feels like it's impossible for them not to be a bunch of violent religious terrorists focused on oppressing Palestinians and propping up the secular State of Israel.<br /> <br /> It's not hard, because the people that created it made if very easy to turn anyone into the bad guys.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444614-so-why-do-the-wendigo-call-themsevles-that-anyway?p=1444964#post1444964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the part where we miss each other is, &quot;What do you mean it's a lie?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>What I mean is that the setting lore has to override real world beliefs; making those beliefs false as a matter of fact in the setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are people playing Wendigo as good guys? </div> </div> </div>Yes, people generally play the Garou as the good guys despite their flaws. WtA fans are not, as a whole, consumed with the VtM struggle over &quot;A monster I am lest a monster I become,&quot; because Garou don't get more monstrous with power, or age, or whatever. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T18:41:48-07:00","id":1444975,"title":"","content":"I understand and apologize for making an offensive comment. I've always leaned into the Technocracy as a Far Right organization due to its continued support of racial supremacist (building a Master Race via the Progenitors), unfettered capitalism (The Syndicate), totalitarianism (which comes in Right Wing and Left Wing you're correct), and information control (New World Order). I've also read into its activity as metaphorical for oppressing religious and racial minorities (The Traditions).<br /> <br /> I suppose I didn't see the Jewish conspiracy theory because I saw them as representing the people oppressing Jews and the worst of Western capitalism and nationalism embodied into a single &quot;The Man&quot; group. The association with Nazis is specifically also, that the Technocracy had a Civil War after half the Convention walked out with the decision to support them before the NEPHANDI co-opted them.<br /> <br /> My bad and I will adjust my opinions accordingly. Thank you for taking the time to correct me, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Satyros Brucato has said that the reason M20 didn't update the Lions of Zion, is because he feels like it's impossible for them not to be a bunch of violent religious terrorists focused on oppressing Palestinians and propping up the secular State of Israel. </div> </div> </div>That is awful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, people generally play the Garou as the good guys despite their flaws. WtA fans are not, as a whole, consumed with the VtM struggle over &quot;A monster I am lest a monster I become,&quot; because Garou don't get more monstrous with power, or age, or whatever. </div> </div> </div>Interesting. I suppose I have always leaned heavily into the anti-hero nature of the Garou in the same way that the Vampire Anarchs are anti-heroes fighting worse beings. For me, using the Wendigo as a name for the Garou instead of a Bane the Garou fight was an acknowledgement that &quot;Cannibal Spirits of the Winter&quot; are how normal human beings would see them.<br /> <br /> I may have been giving them too much credit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-20-2021, 09:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T18:56:10-07:00","id":1444976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444614-so-why-do-the-wendigo-call-themsevles-that-anyway?p=1444964#post1444964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the part where we miss each other is, &amp;quot;What do you mean it's a lie?&amp;quot; I mean, werewolves are monsters who used to conduct a millennia-long genocide. The use of Wendigo as a name is a sign that werewolves are MONSTERS. It's a nice reminder that it is not a purely Western myth. And that their name has gone down in history as a thing to be FEARED.<br /> <br /> Are people playing Wendigo as good guys?<br /> <br /> Unless you are kinfolk, everyone is instinctually afraid of you because you are a creature to be feared.</div> </div> </div> </div>The W word isn\u2019t just a scary monster it is a embodiment of Algonquian equivalent of sin and greed, the pure tribes are said to be very connected to indigenous culture unlike the western werewolves that aren\u2019t at all. Like in Algonquian folklore the creature seems pretty much like a bane. <br /> <br /> And a tribe of Wyrm fighting Garou would totally name themselves after what\u2019s a fucking Bane,<br /> <br /> Plus the technocracy being fascists in first edition doesn\u2019t change the fake that their also based on anti-Semitic stereotypes, we call them caricatures because they have little to do with what actually marginalized groups are like. See all the gay nazi shit despite the fact that Nazis hated gays.<br /> <br /> The \u201cNew World Order\u201d is still being used as a conspiracy theory in alt right circles with heavily antisemtic undertones. <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_World_Order_(conspiracy_theory\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_...spiracy_theory</a>)<br /> <br /> And it was used by that in the 90s to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T19:04:46-07:00","id":1444977,"title":"","content":"Thanks for explaining it.<br /> <br /> I do think we need more anti-fascist works in gaming and World of Darkness has a lot of potential as a social satire one.<br /> <br /> Renaming isn't that hard either as a start.<br /> <br /> The Assamites, Followers of Set, and others have been renamed. Wendigo could be renamed as something more appropriate.<br /> <br /> Even if you have to do a sidebar that says, &quot;Its always been this way. Bear with us.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T19:26:31-07:00","id":1444978,"title":"","content":"Renaming things is a good start, yes, but by itself it really isn't enough. It's solving the most obvious issue, but also the most superficial one. Changing their Totem is a bit more than a naming issue. Trying to shed the Wendigo of their Noble Savage tropes, digging out some of the White Man's Burden mentality in the books were non-indigenous people need to save the Wendigo (or rather, the Wendigo need to &quot;let go of the past&quot; and accept European descendant help), and so on is a much more involved effort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T19:30:18-07:00","id":1444979,"title":"","content":"Plus why do they in-universe call themselves the New World Order? They haven\u2019t been \u201cnew\u201d for a while. And the name seems clearly obvious for a bunch of spies, like the C.I.A doesn\u2019t call itself the Coup governments that America doesn\u2019t like Agency, and despite making a game about the occult and folklore in the modern day their was clearly no research done into folklore and religions especially non western religions and cultures. Plus somehow thinking Set and Aphohis where the same entity despite the fact Set hated Apophis? How did you fail that bad WW<br /> <br /> Indigenous spirituality has a very long history of being distorted in the hegemonic west. Like even anthropological studies get things hideously wrong. Which is why people are criticizing the pure tribes Phipps","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T19:44:31-07:00","id":1444981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444614-so-why-do-the-wendigo-call-themsevles-that-anyway?p=1444978#post1444978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Renaming things is a good start, yes, but by itself it really isn't enough. It's solving the most obvious issue, but also the most superficial one. Changing their Totem is a bit more than a naming issue. Trying to shed the Wendigo of their Noble Savage tropes, digging out some of the White Man's Burden mentality in the books were non-indigenous people need to save the Wendigo (or rather, the Wendigo need to &quot;let go of the past&quot; and accept European descendant help), and so on is a much more involved effort.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be interested in what you would envision the Tribe as afterward.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I suspect this may be why HEART OF THE FOREST suggested the Apocalypse was going to happen. I wouldn't be surprised if the Wendigo, Get of Fenris, and other tribes were going to cease to exist for a more Forsaken-esque write up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444614-so-why-do-the-wendigo-call-themsevles-that-anyway?p=1444979#post1444979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus why do they in-universe call themselves the New World Order? They haven\u2019t been \u201cnew\u201d for a while. And the name seems clearly obvious for a bunch of spies, like the C.I.A doesn\u2019t call itself the Coup governments that America doesn\u2019t like Agency, and despite making a game about the occult and folklore in the modern day their was clearly no research done into folklore and religions especially non western religions and cultures. Plus somehow thinking Set and Aphohis where the same entity despite the fact Set hated Apophis? How did you fail that bad WW</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a bad guy to ask because I always call them the Followers of Apep.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Indigenous spirituality has a very long history of being distorted in the hegemonic west. Like even anthropological studies get things hideously wrong. Which is why people are criticizing the pure tribes Phipps </div> </div> </div>I'm not interested in defending the spiritual distortion, I find that indefensible and wouldn't bother trying. I was talking about how one would patch it in a hopefully respectful way. Specifically the idea that the Wendigo are not someone that should be taken as representative of RL spiritual practices because I feel that if you try to make Native American religious practices into something related to the Garou, you're engaging in the worst sort of cultural appropriation.<br /> <br /> So the idea would be Wendigo would have their own spirituality unrelated to Native mythologies and be demonized for their actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-20-2021, 10:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T20:56:50-07:00","id":1444985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444614-so-why-do-the-wendigo-call-themsevles-that-anyway?p=1444981#post1444981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be interested in what you would envision the Tribe as afterward.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would depend largely on how much leeway I have to change things, and frankly I'm not the person to be doing this anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mind you, I suspect this may be why HEART OF THE FOREST suggested the Apocalypse was going to happen. I wouldn't be surprised if the Wendigo, Get of Fenris, and other tribes were going to cease to exist for a more Forsaken-esque write up. </div> </div> </div>Possible. But, &quot;we can't make a respectful Native American focused Tribe, so we killed them instead,&quot; isn't a good look.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T20:58:42-07:00","id":1444986,"title":"","content":"I wonder if the problem is the racial essentialism of Werewolf to begin with.","signatu