chments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T09:26:38-07:00","id":1445058,"title":"","content":"Yes the whole stat for pure breeding, and it\u2019s sometimes seen as something that\u2019s meant to be stupid and bullshit with the Silver fangs being inbred fuckwits","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T09:34:56-07:00","id":1445060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444614-so-why-do-the-wendigo-call-themsevles-that-anyway?p=1445012#post1445012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how you're thinking the concept of race essentialism should be applied in this case.</div> </div> </div> </div>More like Forsaken.<br /> <br /> Lots and lots of tribes with less focus on ethnicities and more like alliances of septs and political affiliations. The Garou are tens of thousands of years old so literally could have their bloodlines be anywhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T10:20:19-07:00","id":1445068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444614-so-why-do-the-wendigo-call-themsevles-that-anyway?p=1445058#post1445058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes the whole stat for pure breeding, and it\u2019s sometimes seen as something that\u2019s meant to be stupid and bullshit with the Silver fangs being inbred fuckwits</div> </div> </div> </div>Pure Breed is a separate issue that WtA needs to address, but I'm not sure how it applies to the topics here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444614-so-why-do-the-wendigo-call-themsevles-that-anyway?p=1445060#post1445060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More like Forsaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still don't understand. Race essentialism is the concept that human races are accurate observations of real differences between different groups of humans, and that being born to a given race inherently molds humans to specific aptitudes and weaknesses.<br /> <br /> In short, it's bullshit pseudoscience that tries to give racism a foundation in biology that doesn't exist.<br /> <br /> Race isn't really part of WtA in that way. The color of your skin or similar features don't modify your stats. They don't even control what Tribes you can join (though members of said Tribe might use that as a reason to deny you entry, which is different from essentialism as it isn't inherent to the individual).<br /> <br /> What I think your meaning here is something closer to demographic determinism: that is some sociological factor can be used t accurately predict your likeliness of expressing a given trait (in this case being Kin or Garou). Pacific islanders are far less likely to be Kin or Garou because they're extremely far removed from any ancestors that might be one and they live in areas that aren't settled by Garou social units for more recent interbreeding.<br /> <br /> But this appeals rather evenly to white people living in Guam as it does to Samoans.<br /> <br /> One of the things I have mentioned in other threads, is that one of the things WtA should do (but is a huge change) is to make all wild Canids spiritually compatible with the Garou instead of just wolves. This vastly expands the desired range of Garou habitation to cover most of the areas where the setting says Garou aren't natively present (namely Central and South America, sub-Saharan Africa, and Australia w/o needing Mokole magical handwaving).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lots and lots of tribes with less focus on ethnicities and more like alliances of septs and political affiliations. </div> </div> </div>I don't feel this really describes Forsaken's approach to things, or how you could take inspiration from it for fixing WtA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T10:38:17-07:00","id":1445074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444614-so-why-do-the-wendigo-call-themsevles-that-anyway?p=1445068#post1445068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't feel this really describes Forsaken's approach to things, or how you could take inspiration from it for fixing WtA.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we really talked past one another.<br /> <br /> Basically I mean universalizing the tribes and making them so that you could be a Get (perhaps not of Fenris) in Sub Saharan Africa.<br /> <br /> Unlike the tribes from specific racial subgroups and make them ideologies.<br /> <br /> That may go over like a ton of bricks but will allow a more international Garou. You can still have the issues they address like drawing attention to First Nations rights but they'd be done locally at the sept level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T10:55:35-07:00","id":1445077,"title":"","content":"I think using words like ethnicity instead of race might help here.<br /> <br /> Forsaken's approaches to Tribes has Merit, but is unlikely to appeal to WtA fans because the Tribes can feel bland on the surface without the hooks into existing cultures that WtA uses. I really doubt WtA fans would like to see the game turn into WtF's focus on packs as the core social unit of Garou life and all alliances above that becoming conditional and optional.<br /> <br /> I do have thoughts on what I think you're getting at, but it's a rather in-depth post I'll get to when I have more free time.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T11:02:35-07:00","id":1445078,"title":"","content":"Gotcha. Sorry for the confusion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T11:04:29-07:00","id":1445079,"title":"","content":"From my nordic/european perspective, most tribes already do in fact allow international members. I mean, the Fenrir allow Americans to join and aside from 1st ed TB, they do not exclude by skin colour. Bone Gnawers, Glass Walkers, Children of Gaia and Black Furies are pretty much 'everything goes' tribes. Most Striders are not from Egypt, either. Silver Fangs have noble houses all around the world.<br /> <br /> Heck, Rage across the World 20th had Younger Brother hang out with the Masai.<br /> <br /> It does not break the game to have tribes with members not from their 'native' race. In fact, that is very much a -given- since the game was set in America.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T12:50:42-07:00","id":1445103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444614-so-why-do-the-wendigo-call-themsevles-that-anyway?p=1445079#post1445079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From my nordic/european perspective, most tribes already do in fact allow international members. I mean, the Fenrir allow Americans to join and aside from 1st ed TB, they do not exclude by skin colour. Bone Gnawers, Glass Walkers, Children of Gaia and Black Furies are pretty much 'everything goes' tribes. Most Striders are not from Egypt, either. Silver Fangs have noble houses all around the world.<br /> <br /> Heck, Rage across the World 20th had Younger Brother hang out with the Masai.<br /> <br /> It does not break the game to have tribes with members not from their 'native' race. In fact, that is very much a -given- since the game was set in America.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait the first edition tribe book had the get exclude people that went white? No wonder people call them racist.<br /> <br /> But yeah Werewolf has some problematic racial comtemt","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T14:13:59-07:00","id":1445115,"title":"","content":"W:tA explicitly makes a number of indigenous folks around the world who grow up in their respective culture immune to the Delirium, as not every human locale got hunted, most notably the Americas and Australia. This has been the case since 1e, and would ensure that Little Brother being associated with sin and greed would be even more out of place, because even the local non-kin didn't have a long history of being victimized to draw on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444614-so-why-do-the-wendigo-call-themsevles-that-anyway?p=1445074#post1445074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think we really talked past one another.<br /> <br /> Basically I mean universalizing the tribes and making them so that you could be a Get (perhaps not of Fenris) in Sub Saharan Africa.</div> </div> </div> </div>Already possible, pending their ability to not be murdered by more numerous Bastet. Golden jackals are not like other jackals in that they are actually bona fide wolves, as opposed to dire wolves, which were closer to &quot;conventional&quot; jackals, dholes and African wild hunting dogs (both of the latter which support Red Talons populations, courtesy of Mokole lending a helping hand).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Unlike the tribes from specific racial subgroups and make them ideologies.<br /> <br /> That may go over like a ton of bricks but will allow a more international Garou. You can still have the issues they address like drawing attention to First Nations rights but they'd be done locally at the sept level. </div> </div> </div>The Shadow Lords actually have a compromise model that I wish had been implemented - Thunder has one tribe of several distinct branches, as the Shadow Lords in Western Eurasia were just one branch alongside distinct branches Central Asia and also Japan/East Asia. The Get of Fenris could be similarly divvied up among, to give an example, South Asia (based on legends of Rahu, another monster wolf that tries to eat the moon) and East Asia (based on legends of Tiangou, a dark wolf-like creature that tries to eat the moon and namesake of the Japanese Tengu). Basically, if there's a legend of a giant wolf that tries to eat the moon, the Fenrir can and probably should have a presence there. Similarly, the Black Furies and Children of Gaia can work off of different locales' legends of winged horses and unicorns., respectively; Hengeyokai, for all its faults, even mentions the latter as a reason why there were CoGgies in the Beast Courts, prior to the terrible retcons of Blood and Silk.<br /> <br /> And now that I've mentioned that book, I have to go and vainly write another conversion of 2e Alchemical Charms into Lunar ones to work off the Rage. Fucking Blood and Silk...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T14:31:52-07:00","id":1445121,"title":"","content":"What did blood and silk retcon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T14:57:17-07:00","id":1445130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444614-so-why-do-the-wendigo-call-themsevles-that-anyway?p=1445103#post1445103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait the first edition tribe book had the get exclude people that went white? No wonder people call them racist.<br /> <br /> But yeah Werewolf has some problematic racial comtemt</div> </div> </div> </div>There was a lot of racial matters done....poorly, early on.<br /> <br /> Evan Heals the Past is the first white Wendigo and went over like a ton of bricks for....obvious reasons. The white kid should not be the one trying to reconcile indigenous and colonializer descended people.<br /> <br /> I think he makes a fine Child of Gaia, though, and nicely addresses how bloodlines of Garou can lay dormant for a long time. But even with him, if he'd been biracial instead of looking all white he probably would have been received differently.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> [Reposted from V20 vs. V5]<br /> <br /> The sad fact is that White Wolf and the World of Darkness have actually had to deal with white supremacist appropriatioin several times in the past. One of the most famous incidents being the Sword of Heimdall one in Werewolf: The Apocalypse. Ethan Skemp, way back when, basically said that they had a white supremacy problem among Werewolf: The Apocalypse &quot;fans&quot; with it being appropriated by them and people showing up at LARPs or games claiming to be just playing in character while embracing the (meant to be villains) Swords of Heimdall. This is notably why the Werewolf camp was exterminated to the last Garou in Werewolf Revised.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-21-2021, 06:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T17:00:02-07:00","id":1445159,"title":"","content":"Weren\u2019t the Swords of hermidl meant to be the token evil camp like does Coggies that worship the Wyrm. But they\u2019re also super cool werewolf\u2019s fighting against \u201cdedgretes\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T18:02:30-07:00","id":1445165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444614-so-why-do-the-wendigo-call-themsevles-that-anyway?p=1445159#post1445159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weren\u2019t the Swords of hermidl meant to be the token evil camp like does Coggies that worship the Wyrm. But they\u2019re also super cool werewolf\u2019s fighting against \u201cdedgretes\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>They were the designated &quot;scumbag&quot; camp but they were listed in the same section as the Players options. So, obviously white supremacist &quot;fans&quot; were going to latch onto them.<br /> <br /> Especially as Werewolf unfortunately had already been attracting some white supremacist gamers drawn in by other elements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-e