ref=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444614-so-why-do-the-wendigo-call-themsevles-that-anyway?p=1445121#post1445121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What did blood and silk retcon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Tribes other than Hakken and Stargazers among the Beast Courts, as in, it seemed to forget that they existed and insisted that the reader forget, too. In particular, it made Chiyou, the foe of the Yellow Emperor, a Hakken, and the Yellow Emperor into one of the by then corrupted Wan Xian. Afterwards, Chiyou becomes the only Garou to be imprisoned in the same hell that the Gui Ren souls occupy before returning to their bodies.<br /> <br /> It was all thoroughly unnecessary, built up no heat, and created a confusion in timing of events. Exactly what one would expect from a book that purports to know about Chinese Romanization, but only lists two styles, and incorrectly attributes the reading of Peking to Yale-style, which did not exist at the time that reading of those characters was valid.<br /> <br /> (Yale has never known a reading of Beijing other than Beijing; Wade-Giles and Legge, however...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}